        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Logistics manage inter-island execution: booking, vessel/roro schedule, port handling, drayage at origin/destination (links to W222/W3503), customs/domestic-trade documentation where applicable (links to VS-87), and in-transit visibility (W3508); manage island-specific disruption (typhoon links to VS-69, port congestion)
Responsible (R): Logistics / Shipping Line / Forwarder
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Per shipment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3510_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3510_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3510_Task6" name="Logistics/Finance capture inter-island freight cost (higher per-unit than…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Logistics/Finance capture inter-island freight cost (higher per-unit than intra-region), allocate to the destination island/DC/store (links to VS-72/W3514), feed landed cost (W3515) and cost-to-serve (W3516), and report inter-island service/cost performance (W3512); optimize network (DC catchment links to VS-04)
Responsible (R): Logistics / Finance
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3510_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3510_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
