    <bpmn:process id="W_W3511" name="W3511. Freight Claims, Loss &amp; Damage Recovery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Loss/damage/shortage in transit (links to VS-90); delivery discrepancy
Frequency: Event-driven
Volume: Freight claims across all legs
Owner: Logistics / Claims
Participants: Logistics (links to VS-06/VS-90), DC/Store (links to VS-04/VS-07), Carrier/3PL (links to VS-56), Insurance (links to VS-26), AP/AR (links to VS-15/VS-16), Legal (links to VS-100)
Source: workflow W3511 — Freight Claims, Loss &amp; Damage Recovery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3511_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3511_Lane1" name="DC">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3511_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3511_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3511_Lane2" name="Logistics">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3511_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3511_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3511_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3511_Start4" name="Loss/damage/shortage in transit (links to VS-90); delivery discrepancy">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3511_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3511_Task5" name="DC/Store/Logistics detect and document the in-transit loss/damage/shortage at…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: DC/Store/Logistics detect and document the in-transit loss/damage/shortage at receipt (links to VS-04.1/W1366/VS-07.3) or customer delivery (links to W1372/VS-90): photos, POD/exception, shipment/con note, quantity/value, and notice to the carrier within the claim window (links to VS-90 short windows)
Responsible (R): DC / Store / Logistics
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3511_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3511_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3511_Task6" name="Logistics/Claims file the freight claim with the carrier/3PL (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Logistics/Claims file the freight claim with the carrier/3PL (links to VS-90/W3017): claim form, supporting docs, liability per contract (W3499) and CMR/domestic rules, and negotiation; escalate to insurance (links to VS-26.3/W59) for unrecovered/consequential loss and to legal (links to VS-100) for disputes
Responsible (R): Logistics / Claims / Carrier / Insurance
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3511_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3511_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3511_Task7" name="Logistics/AP-AR settle the claim: carrier credit/refund, insurance recovery…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Logistics/AP-AR settle the claim: carrier credit/refund, insurance recovery (links to VS-26.3), write-off of unrecovered loss (links to VS-35/VS-05.3), and GL posting (links to VS-17); feed claims analytics (W3516), carrier scorecard (W3512), and root-cause/capa (links to VS-90/VS-31)
Responsible (R): Logistics / AP-AR / Finance
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager / CFO
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3511_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3511_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3511_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3511_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3511_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-78 (ensure freight invoice accuracy &amp; carrier compliance.) | - operational: receipt-time detection and prompt filing; operational: insurance and contract liability terms
Owner: Logistics / Claims</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
